  "id": "Compound::DB00211 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Midodrine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Adra1d, which is a splice variant of the Adra1 gene. This binding is linked to the participation of Adra1d in the Alpha1-adrenergic receptor activity, a function that is also shared by Adra1b. The evidence suggests that Midodrine may influence Adra1b through its interaction with Adra1d, potentially modulating the Alpha1-adrenergic receptor activity. The overlapping roles of Adra1d and Adra1b in the Alpha1-adrenergic receptor pathway imply a possible functional relationship between Midodrine and Adra1b, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The consistent binding to Adra1d and its involvement in the same pathway as Adra1b provide a plausible basis for the observed relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct functional link between Midodrine and Adra1b.",
